WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
An early Buddhist text lists
four things to watch closely:

2
00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:09.240
the body, feelings, the
mind, and mental qualities.

3
00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.750
Breathing in.

4
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.280
Breathing out.

5
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.830
A pleasant feeling.

6
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.540
An unpleasant one.

7
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.370
A wandering thought.

8
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:19.890
The meditator does not chase any of them,

9
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.540
or push them away.

10
00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:25.860
They simply watch,
closely, moment by moment.

11
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.230
Can watching your own breath and itches
really show you the truth about who you

12
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.270
are?

13
00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.670
In this mission, you'll meet insight
meditation, called vipassana.

14
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.450
Then you'll see how mindfulness
runs through ethics,

15
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.110
calm and daily life, as one
factor of the Eightfold Path.

16
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.800
Your mission: find out what close
watching can show you about who you are.
